      "writtenOn": "2017-01-19T22:38:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think is possible to simplify the subtraction and selection a little bit if you want. The end result is something like this:\n\n// h + -p\nt0 :\u003d h0 + 5\nt1 :\u003d h1 + (t0 \u003e\u003e 26)\nt0 \u0026\u003d 0x3ffffff\nt2 :\u003d h2 + (t1 \u003e\u003e 26)\nt3 :\u003d h3 + (t2 \u003e\u003e 26)\nt4 :\u003d h4 + (t3 \u003e\u003e 26)\n\n// select h if h \u003c p else h + -p\nh_mask :\u003d (t4 \u003e\u003e 26) - 1\nt_mask :\u003d ^h_mask\nh0 \u003d (h0 \u0026 h_mask) | (t0 \u0026 t_mask)\nh1 \u003d (h1 \u0026 h_mask)\nh2 \u003d (h2 \u0026 h_mask)\nh3 \u003d (h3 \u0026 h_mask)\nh4 \u003d (h4 \u0026 h_mask)\n\nThis change relies on two observations:\n\n1. t will only be selected if it is in the range [0,5) (since h has been reduced to 130 bits already).\n2. h + (-p%(2^130)) can only carry 1 bit, which will end up in position 26 of h4.",
      "revId": "a126ec508a23e7d58c7686ab8b300c1a352c82da",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
